<title>NETHERLANDS: Stork's Fokker Elmo in Chinese venture.</title>
<headline>Stork's Fokker Elmo in Chinese venture.</headline>
<dateline>NAARDEN, Netherlands 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial systems and services group Stork NV said Fokker Elmo, a unit of its affiliate Fokker Aviation, had signed a joint venture contract with two units of Aviations Industries of China (AVIC).  </p>
<p>The joint venture, named Lang Fang Fokker Corp and 60-percent owned by Fokker Elmo, will produce electric wiring for both the Chinese and western aviation sector.</p>
<p>&quot;The joint venture's sales is expected to grow to an annual 80 million guilders within five years,&quot; Stork said in a statement.</p>
<p>The new company would also develop complete electric systems for Chinese aircraft development programmes such as the 100-seat Regioliner, Stork said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
